# E13's Gemma arm (A73): Gemma 4 12B as the local judge, in place of ~/llm/llm.env (copy it over, then
# `systemctl --user restart llm-judge`; the Qwen file goes back the same way). Same server settings as llm.env; only
# the model and its model-specific flags differ. No secrets here (the API key lives in ~/.config/llm/secret.env).
# Google's quantisation-aware-trained 4-bit checkpoint (int4 weights, 16-bit activations; ≈ 9.6 GB)
JUDGE_MODEL=google/gemma-4-12B-it-qat-w4a16-ct
JUDGE_PORT=8000
JUDGE_GPU_SHARE=0.92
JUDGE_MAX_LEN=8192
# 2,048 (llm.env: 4,096): Gemma's 1,024-token sliding-window layers hold the window plus one prefill chunk, and with
# 4,096 the first start (while compiling) left too little room for one 8 k request; the cache holds ≈ 12 k tokens either way
JUDGE_BATCH_TOKENS=2048
VLLM_USE_FLASHINFER_SAMPLER=0
# model-specific flags: text only (no image/audio inputs, so none are profiled or reserved); no reasoning parser — the
# judge runs with thinking off, and Gemma's template then closes the thought channel in the prompt, so the strict JSON
# schema applies from the first answer token. LoRA modules are added per experiment (--lora-modules name=path).
JUDGE_EXTRA_ARGS=--language-model-only --structured-outputs-config.backend xgrammar --structured-outputs-config.disable_any_whitespace true --enable-lora --max-lora-rank 16
